Apple today <a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/2026/11/apple-reports-fourth-quarter-results/">announced</a> financial results for the fourth fiscal quarter of 2026, which corresponds to the third calendar quarter of the year. The quarter included a number of August and September product releases from Apple, as well as the CEO transition from <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/tim-cook/">Tim Cook</a> to John Ternus that took place on September 1.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/aapl-4q26-line.jpg" alt="" width="1726" height="766" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1075213" /><br/>
For the quarter, Apple posted revenue of &#36;114.5 billion and net quarterly profit of &#36;30.7 billion, or &#36;2.10 per diluted share, compared to revenue of &#36;102.5 billion and net quarterly profit of &#36;27.5 billion, or &#36;1.85 per diluted share, in the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/10/30/apple-4q-2025-earnings/">year-ago quarter</a>.<br/>
<br/>
Gross margin for the most recent quarter was 47.9 percent, compared to 47.2 percent in the year-ago quarter. Apple also declared a quarterly dividend payment of &#36;0.27 per share, payable on November 16 to shareholders of record as of November 12.<br/>
<br/>
Apple set September quarter records for total revenue, iPhone revenue, and earnings per share, and an all-time record for Services revenue.<br/>
<br/>
For the full fiscal year, Apple recorded &#36;478.8 billion in sales and &#36;132.2 billion in net income, compared to previous record highs of &#36;416.2 billion in sales and &#36;112.0 billion in net income set in fiscal 2025.<blockquote>"Today, Apple is proud to report a September quarter revenue record of &#36;114.5 billion, up 12 percent from a year ago, with iPhone reaching a September quarter record and Services reaching an all-time high, capping off our best fiscal year ever," said John Ternus, Apple's CEO. "We're closing the year with our most ambitious lineup yet. That includes the iPhone Duo, the most transformational iPhone since the original, alongside iPhone 18 Pro and iPhone 18 Pro Max, our most powerful iPhones yet. We also just introduced a whole new generation of hardware for the home and brought Touch to Mac for the first time. Together with the all-new Siri AI, it's an incredible lineup to carry us into the holiday season."</blockquote><br/>
